<title>UK: LIFFE sugar stays quiet, mixed in PM trade.</title>
<headline>LIFFE sugar stays quiet, mixed in PM trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>LIFFE sugar was mixed in still lacklustre afternoon trading.</p>
<p>&quot;It was a grim morning and it's been followed by a grim afternoon,&quot; one trader said. He described the market as &quot;unbelievably dead.&quot;</p>
<p>By 1530 GMT, 530 lots had changed hands, 308 on front month August. It most recently traded at $320.40, 30 cents lower.</p>
<p>There was no fundamental news driving the market, traders said.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
